          "label": "<p>A CSF Gram stain shows kidney-shaped organisms arranged in pairs, some located w</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A CSF Gram stain shows kidney-shaped organisms arranged in pairs, some located within neutrophils. What is the correct identification?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Gram-positive Streptococcus pneumoniae</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>S. pneumoniae appears as lancet-shaped, Gram-positive diplococci — a distinctly different morphology. Kidney-shaped intracellular diplococci point to a Gram-negative organism.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Gram-negative Neisseria meningitidis</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Kidney-shaped diplococci found intracellularly within neutrophils are the hallmark CSF Gram stain appearance of N. meningitidis. This pattern enables immediate bedside diagnosis and guides empiric ceftriaxone therapy.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Gram-negative Escherichia coli</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>E. coli appears as Gram-negative bacilli (rods), not kidney-shaped diplococci. E. coli meningitis occurs predominantly in neonates with the K1 capsular antigen.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Gram-positive Staphylococcus aureus</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Staphylococci are Gram-positive cocci arranged in grape-like clusters, typically seen in post-neurosurgical or shunt-related meningitis — not as kidney-shaped diplococci.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Learn the two key diplococcal patterns: kidney-shaped Gram-negative intracellular diplococci = N. meningitidis; lancet-shaped Gram-positive diplococci = S. pneumoniae."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Excellent! Recognising organism-specific Gram stain morphology enables bedside diagnosis within minutes — often life-saving in bacterial meningitis."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
                "enableRetry": true,
                "enableSolutionsButton": true,
